  "summary": "Talk about pollution, rubbish, recycling and the climate, say what we must do with يَجِبُ أَنْ and مِنَ اللَّازِمِ أَنْ, and plan a clean-up day with the class.",
  "intro": "Week 12 is about society and the world, and it opens with the environment, الْبِيئَة. Today you will talk about pollution (تَلَوُّث), rubbish (نُفَايَات), recycling (إِعَادَةُ التَّدْوِير) and the climate (الْمُنَاخ). To say what we must do, use يَجِبُ أَنْ or مِنَ اللَّازِمِ أَنْ (it is necessary to) + a verb ending in -a: يَجِبُ أَنْ نَحْمِيَ الْبِيئَةَ (we must protect the environment). In everyday speech you will also hear لَازِم أَنْ; in writing, use these forms. Many of today's words are verbal nouns: إِعَادَةُ التَّدْوِير is literally 'doing the turning again', and يَوْمُ تَنْظِيفٍ is 'a day of cleaning', a clean-up day. Listen for the ḍād (ض) in الْأَرْضُ (the earth) and مُضِرّ (harmful).",
  "objectives": [
    "Name environmental problems: pollution, rubbish and climate change",
    "Say what we must do with يَجِبُ أَنْ or مِنَ اللَّازِمِ أَنْ + a verb ending in -a",
    "Use verbal nouns like إِعَادَةُ التَّدْوِير (recycling) and حِمَايَةُ الْبِيئَةِ (protecting the environment)",
    "Give simple advice on saving water and energy at home"
  ],
